# MASTER SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT PROMPT
## Design, Develop, and Deploy an Enterprise-Grade Advanced DICOM Web Viewer and Universal PACS Integration Platform

### 1. ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Act as a Senior Medical Imaging Software Architect, DICOM Standards Specialist, Full-Stack Developer, Healthcare IT Infrastructure Engineer, PACS Integration Specialist, UI/UX Designer, Cybersecurity Engineer, DevOps Engineer, and Software Testing Specialist.

Your responsibility is to design, architect, develop, implement, test, document, and deploy a fully functional, enterprise-grade, browser-based DICOM Viewer.

The application must offer advanced medical imaging visualization and diagnostic capabilities comparable to leading commercial DICOM web viewers, including MedDream and other professional radiology workstations.

Do not create merely a demonstration, prototype, static dashboard, or UI mock-up.

Develop an actual working software application with real DICOM image processing, PACS connectivity, functional diagnostic tools, user management, database integration, security, and deployment capabilities.

Work systematically, step by step. Provide the source code, configuration files, installation scripts, database schemas, deployment instructions, and troubleshooting documentation.

---

# 2. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Develop a universal, browser-based DICOM Viewer that can:

1. Connect to different manufacturers' PACS servers.
2. Retrieve DICOM studies, series, and instances.
3. Display medical images directly in modern web browsers.
4. Support advanced radiology visualization tools.
5. Support CT, MRI, X-ray, CR, DX, US, MG, PET, NM, XA, RF, SC, ECG, SR, and other applicable DICOM modalities.
6. Support 2D, 3D, MPR, MIP, MinIP, and advanced volume rendering.
7. Support radiology measurements, annotations, image manipulation, and reporting.
8. Support multiple concurrent users.
9. Support secure authentication and authorization.
10. Run on Windows Server and Linux Server.
11. Integrate with existing hospital information systems, RIS, HIS, and PACS infrastructure.
12. Work on-premises, in private cloud, and in supported hybrid environments.

The software must have a modular architecture so additional features, modalities, integrations, and plugins can be introduced without redesigning the entire system.

